    "text": "The goat was a symbolic animal for the Celts. Evidence shows the goat was sacred and useful for sacrifice. A curse kept goats away from the abbey at Kildare. That site was first a place of Celtic worship. The goat may stand for the male force. Women held the sanctuary, so men could not enter. The horned god Cernunnos had goat's legs but stag's horns. The male goat is famed for its sexuality. Christian art shows the Devil as goat-footed. It does this to mock the male sexual force.",
